session Geometric_Viscosity_Comparison = Second_Order_Viscosity_Analysis +
  description "
    Comparison principles for viscosity solutions of F(Du, D^2 u) = 1 for
    any second-order operator F on R^n x R^(n x n) in the locale
    geometric_operator: degenerate ellipticity, positive homogeneity in the
    Hessian, invariance under positive dilations of the gradient and under
    rotations, a bound on the effect of shifting the Hessian by a multiple
    of the identity, agreement with both semicontinuous envelopes off a
    vanishing gradient and with the lower one at a vanishing gradient, and
    the upper envelope below 1 at (0, 0) and uniformly at (q, -delta I).
    For such an operator: the semicontinuous envelopes of an operator and
    their invariances; strict subsolutions by scaling; the contradiction
    between second-order jets of the sup-convolutions of a subsolution and
    a supersolution at a maximiser of the doubled functional; the maximum
    principle for an upper semicontinuous subsolution and a lower
    semicontinuous supersolution on a bounded set, which may degenerate
    where the gradient vanishes; comparison between two domains, comparison
    and uniqueness on expandable sets, and uniqueness on compact sets.
    Built on Second_Order_Viscosity_Analysis for the doubling of variables,
    the sup-convolution, Jensen's lemma and the viscosity notions, and on
    Semicontinuous_Analysis for semicontinuity and envelopes.
  "
  options [document = pdf, document_output = "output"]
  sessions
    Semicontinuous_Analysis
  theories
    Geometric_Operator
    Comparison_Strictness
    Comparison_Localisation
    Maximum_Principle
    Comparison_Two_Domain
  theories [document = false]
    No_Probability_Or_Paper_Ancestor
  document_files
    "root.tex"
    "root.bib"
